{
  "version": 8,
  "title": "Daily Summary",
  "description": "The AI-composed end-of-day review (span `day_summary.generate`, service meridian-rust). ONE centralised LLM call reads the day's evidence (`day_evidence.collect`) and answers with a narrative, a few insights, and 2-4 raw Vega-Lite specs it chose itself. The model picks the FORM; it never supplies a NUMBER - every spec binds its data by name and the real rows are injected at render, so a hallucinated figure has nowhere to live.\n\nWHAT TO WATCH: `fallback` is the report card. Raw Vega-Lite emission was chosen over a constrained schema, which means no provider is correct by construction and validity rests entirely on validation + fallback. A rising fallback rate, or `drop_reasons` clustering on `vega_lite_schema`, is the signal that the decision needs revisiting (the answer would be a narrower schema, not more retries - there is no repair loop, on purpose: a second call would double a ~1 minute action's latency).\n\n`drop_reasons` tags: vega_lite_schema (failed the real grammar) | inline_data (tried to supply its own numbers) | unknown_dataset | unknown_field | missing_data_name. Each row's full trace carries the llm.request(prompt+input)/llm.response(output) subspans. Click a row for the trace.",
  "variables": {
    "list": [],
    "showDynamicFilters": true
  },
  "defaultDatetimeDuration": {
    "type": "relative",
    "relativeTimePeriod": "24h"
  },
